  "passage": "Last November, I decided to take a short holiday to the seaside town of Brightling. It was the furthest I had ever traveled on my own, so I felt both nervous and thrilled. My primary object for the trip was complete relaxation, as I had been studying hard for exams. The hotel I booked had a modern design, which was surprising for such an old town. On my first attempt to explore, I walked to the historic pier, but it started raining badly. I quickly went to a cosy café and treated myself to a warm cup of tea and a large chocolate cookie. I definitely deserved it after the long journey! The next day, the weather was clear, and I spent the day in a nearby forest, which was perfect for unwinding. Overall, it was a refreshing break that I needed.",
